","party":"PRES","person_id":"tvfy_10507","person_slug":"stephen-parry","vote":"no"},{"name":"Sue Lines","party":"PRES","person_id":"tvfy_10782","person_slug":"sue-lines","vote":"no"}],"name":"Motions - Canberra Airport - Weapons advertisements","noes":43,"question":"The majority voted against a [motion](http://www.openaustralia.org.au/senate/?id=2016-03-01.115.1) introduced by Greens Senator for NSW [Lee Rhiannon](https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/people/senate/nsw/lee_rhiannon), which means it failed. ### Motion text > *That the Senate—* > *(a) notes that:* >> *(i) Canberra Airport currently displays large and prominent advertisements by some of the world's biggest weapons manufacturers,* >> *(ii) weapons of war are inappropriate images to greet visitors to our national capital, especially with direct international flights to Canberra to begin later in 2016, and* >> *(iii) Canberra and Australia should be identified to visitors as places of unique historical, natural and cultural attractions, and not as primarily concerned with war machinery;* > *(b) congratulates the more than 1,500 citizens from Canberra and elsewhere who have petitioned Canberra Airport Management to remove the weapons advertisements; and* > *(c) supports their campaign to remove the weapons advertisements.*","result":"negative","slug":"division-federal-senate-4109","source_url":"https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/divisions/senate/2016-03-01/2"}
